..pull-request-footer:
**After merging**, the `release-please` workflow run on `main` (about 5 minutes):
1. tags the version and creates its GitHub release;
2. builds the CLI for four platforms and attaches the archives and `SHA256SUMS` (`release.yml`);
3. builds both images with werf and pushes them to Docker Hub, `koblas/exemplar` and `koblas/exemplar-learning`, as `<x.y.z>`, `<x.y>` and `latest` (`images.yml`);
4. attaches `install-tunnel.yaml` and `install-direct.yaml`, pinned to those image digests (`manifests.yml`).

Then check that the run is green and the release has its assets, and upgrade installations by pinning the new digests: [Releases and images](https://koblas.github.io/exemplar/reference/releases/).

Maintained by [release-please](https://github.com/googleapis/release-please); process in [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/koblas/exemplar/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md#releasing).
